---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Summary from '../components/Summary.astro';
import Divider from '../components/Divider.astro';
---
<Base title={"Therapy for Teens in Provo & Utah County | Tangible Therapy"} description={"Teen therapy in Orem, Provo, & Sandy. A judgment-free, LGBTQ+ affirming space for anxiety, depression, identity & life changes. Free 15-min consult."}>
<section class="sec t-bright h-medium has-bg has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-bg"><img src="/images/tangible-72-3fd73d.jpg" alt="" style="object-position:51% 9%" loading="eager"><div class="sec-ov" style="opacity:0.42"></div></div><div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:7;--mrows:10">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/5/6/23;--m:1/2/7/10"><div class="rte"><h1 class="ta-center">Therapy for Teens</h1><p class="lg ta-center">Support for when everything feels overwhelming.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:6/10/8/18;--m:8/2/10/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Start Teen Therapy Today</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#fff" /></section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:12;--mrows:19">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/6/12;--m:2/2/4/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>Because being a teenager is really hard</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/16/12/26;--m:12/2/19/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-teen-d11a2d.jpg" alt="A teen boy sits across from a therapist in a therapy office in Utah surrounded by plants" width="2500" height="1932" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:6/2/11/12;--m:4/2/12/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>Between academic pressure, social media, shifting identities, family dynamics, and nonstop stress, today’s teens carry a lot. Anxiety, depression, and burnout are rising, and many teens don’t know where to turn.</p><p>At Tangible Therapy, we offer a space to be real, feel heard, and receive honest, respectful, and helpful support.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:15;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:2/2/16/13;--m:13/2/20/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-teen-girl-f21a61.jpg" alt="A teen girl in a brown shirt sits on a couch across from a therapist in a Tangible therapy office in Orem, Utah with a plant in the background" width="3300" height="2550" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/15/6/26;--m:2/2/5/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>We work with teens who are navigating:</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/15/16/25;--m:5/2/13/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><ul><li><p>Anxiety, panic, or social pressure</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Depression or emotional numbness</p></li><li><p>Identity or self-esteem struggles</p></li><li><p>School stress, burnout, or perfectionism</p></li><li><p>Friendship drama or relationship issues</p></li><li><p>Family conflict or communication breakdown</p></li><li><p>Grief, trauma, or big life changes</p></li><li><p>Questions about gender, sexuality, or spirituality</p></li></ul><p>Teens don’t have to be in crisis to benefit from therapy. Sometimes, they need someone other than a parent, teacher, or peer who will listen without judgment.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-black h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:18">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/3/5/12;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2>For parents and caregivers</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-image jc" style="--d:1/14/13/25;--m:9/2/16/10;--dz:4;--mz:4"><figure class="img fill" style="--r:50px"><img src="/images/tangible-74-2e0802.jpg" alt="A teen girl in a brown shirt sits on a couch across from a therapist and her parent in a Tangible therapy office in Provo, Utah with plants in the background" width="2484" height="1866" loading="lazy" decoding="async"></figure></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:5/3/12/12;--m:3/2/10/10;--dz:3;--mz:3"><div class="rte"><p>We know it’s hard to watch your teen struggle. You want to help, but they may not want to talk to you or even understand what they’re feeling. We partner with families while still honoring your teen’s privacy, autonomy, and developmental needs.</p><p>You’ll be looped in when needed and supported through the process, too.</p></div></div>
  <div class="b b-button jc" style="--d:12/3/14/9;--m:16/2/18/10;--dz:5;--mz:5"><div class="btn-wrap ta-center"><a class="btn btn-primary btn-medium btn-full" href="/contact">Schedule A Teen Consultation</a></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-light h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:16;--mrows:7">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/7/3/22;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">Therapists for Teenagers</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-summary-v2" style="--d:3/5/17/24;--m:3/2/8/10"><Summary kind="team" design="carousel" category="telehealth/teens" limit={9} perRow={3} rounded /></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-custom">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top: calc(1vmax / 10); padding-bottom: calc(1vmax / 10);">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:4;--mrows:7">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/8/4/20;--m:2/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">What your teen will get</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:4/4/5/24;--m:4/2/8/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><p class="ta-center">Teen therapy at Tangible is built on respect, privacy, and trust. We don’t lecture, diagnose, or dismiss. Instead, we offer real tools to help teens.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:3;--mrows:3">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:1/4/3/24;--m:1/2/3/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="rte"><p class="ta-center">We tailor each session to the teen’s needs, pace, and personality. Whether it’s talking through big feelings, learn coping skills, or simply being heard, we’re here for it.</p></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>

<section class="sec t-bright-inverse h-small has-div" style="--divh:6vw">
<div class="sec-in" style="padding-top:1vmax;padding-bottom:0vmax">
<div class="wrap"><ul class="ulist ulist-carousel" style="--per:3;--ar:3/2;--tfs:calc((2.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--bfs:calc((1.2 - 1) * var(--fs-unit) + 1rem);--cw:75%;--gap:20px"><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="#" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Learn to regulate emotions</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Learn to express yourself&nbsp; clearly</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Set boundaries and manage relationships</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Understand your identity and values</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Cope with anxiety, depression, or overwhelm</p></div></div></li><li class="li"><a class="li-link" href="/" aria-label="✺"></a><div class="li-body"><h3 class="li-title">✺</h3><div class="rte li-desc"><p>Reconnect with who you are outside of pressure and expectation</p></div></div></li></ul><div class="carousel-nav"><button class="prev" aria-label="Previous"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19 12H5m6-6-6 6 6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button><button class="next" aria-label="Next"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="28" height="28" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 12h14m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg></button></div></div>
</div>
<Divider type="wavy" height={6} width={100} fill="#acb9ac" /></section>

<section class="sec t-black h-medium">
<div class="sec-in">
<div class="fe" style="--rows:13;--mrows:20">
  <div class="b b-html" style="--d:2/2/4/26;--m:1/2/4/10"><div class="rte"><h2 class="ta-center">✺ Frequently asked questions ✺</h2></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/2/14/13;--m:5/2/13/10"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>How old does my teen need to be to start therapy?</summary><div class="rte"><p>We typically work with teens ages 13 and up. If your teen is younger, reach out — we may be able to recommend someone or offer alternate support options.</p></div></details><details><summary>Do parents attend the first session?</summary><div class="rte"><p>That depends on the teen’s age and preference. Sometimes, a parent joins for the start of the first session to discuss goals or background, and then the therapist meets one-on-one with the teen. We’ll guide that process based on what’s best for everyone.</p></div></details><details><summary>Is what my teen says in therapy private?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Yes — with a few exceptions. What your teen shares is confidential unless there’s a safety concern. We work to earn their trust and keep parents appropriately informed when it’s helpful and necessary.</p></div></details></div></div>
  <div class="b b-accordion" style="--d:6/15/12/26;--m:13/2/21/10;--dz:2;--mz:2"><div class="accordion"><details><summary>What if my teen doesn’t want to go?</summary><div class="rte"><p>That’s common. We don’t force it—but we do invite teens into a space where they’re treated with respect and allowed to open up at their own pace. Sometimes all it takes is one good conversation to change their mind.</p></div></details><details><summary>Can you support LGBTQ+ teens or those questioning their identity?</summary><div class="rte"><p>Absolutely. We are fully LGBTQ+ affirming and experienced in helping teens explore gender, sexuality, and identity in a safe, nonjudgmental space.</p></div></details></div></div>
</div>
</div>
</section>
</Base>
